finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-8k.1--plan","local_name":"sase-8k.1--plan","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-8k","agent_clan_generation":"20260722105427","agent_family":"sase-8k.1","agent_family_role":"plan","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-8k.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-8k[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Hidden agents sidecar repo with machine agent hoods[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]Every sase-managed project gains a hidden `<project>--agents` [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]sidecar repo that publicly (or privately, by config) stores the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]data needed to reconstruct every sase agent that created a commit [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]for that project; agent names become globally unique via required [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]machine agent hoods; syncing is wired into `sase repo init`, the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`,U` comprehensive update, a cheap periodic per-project check, and [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]a distinct top-right TUI indicator.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase/repos/plans/202607/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]agents_sidecar_repo.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]machine_name config and sase config init[/bold #D7AFFF]                      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]machine-config[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'machine_name config and sase config init' section: add the required [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]machine_name schema field, machine-local identity selection for [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sase_<machine>.yml overlays, the interactive `sase config init` command [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF](chezmoi-aware writes), and `sase init`/doctor wiring.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust core machine-hood helpers[/bold #D7AFFF]                                [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]core-hood-helpers[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Rust core machine-hood helpers' section: add qualify/strip/validate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]machine-hood functions to sase_core, expose them through pyo3 bindings, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and cover them with unit and parity tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Machine agent hoods end to end[/bold #D7AFFF]                                [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]machine-hoods[dim] · [dim][/dim]after machine-config, core-hood-helpers[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Machine agent hoods end to end' section: qualify new agent names with [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the local machine hood when written to disk, enforce hood-aware [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]uniqueness with legacy-name equivalence, strip the local hood across [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]every display/prompt/lookup surface, and record machine-aware commit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]footers.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Hidden agents sidecar foundation[/bold #D7AFFF]                              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]sidecar-foundation[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Hidden agents sidecar foundation' section: introduce the intrinsically [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]hidden `agents` sidecar role, default injection for sase-managed [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]projects, the machine-level clone location under ~/.sase, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]project-local disable/visibility controls.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase repo init integration[/bold #D7AFFF]                                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]repo-init[dim] · [dim][/dim]after sidecar-foundation[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'sase repo init integration' section: create, seed, and clone the agents[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sidecar during `sase repo init` behind a loud, explicit confirmation [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]that all commit-associated agent chats will be pushed to the new repo.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Agents sync engine and CLI[/bold #D7AFFF]                                    [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]sync-engine[dim] · [dim][/dim]after machine-hoods, repo-init[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'Agents sync engine and CLI' section: implement the per-agent bundle [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]format, the pull -> integrate -> export -> commit -> push sync flow with[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]locking and retries, historical backfill from commit footers, and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`sase agent sync` command.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]TUI sync checks, indicator, and update keymap leg[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]tui-sync[dim] · [dim][/dim]after sync-engine[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'TUI sync checks, indicator, and update keymap leg' section: add the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cheap periodic per-project sync-status check, the distinct top-right [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sync indicator widget, and the agents leg of the `,U` comprehensive [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]update.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]End-to-end exercises and docs[/bold #D7AFFF]                                 [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]smoke[dim] · [dim][/dim]after tui-sync[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]'End-to-end exercises and docs' section: exercise the full flow end to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]end across two simulated machines and finish user-facing documentation.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-8k","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","phase_bead_id":"sase-8k.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","role_suffix":"plan","vcs_provider":"GitHub","workflow_name":"sase-8k.1"},"source_run_id":"run-bc2b3c5c4dd1ee32aeb701db4a88c15b","started_at":"2026-07-22T14:54:34.817747+00:00","state":"active"},{"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"9e8aaf995aae5ee0c312be1e476d528e27f03f0f7f80ab92818f719c7b1df8e7","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-8k.6--plan/chat.md","size_bytes":2217},"commits":{"digest":"1567e93bbc5c46df2f3f3d89d080303ee7d25e48a45c3c44d3cbcb51b9556cf5","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-8k.6--plan/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-8k.6--plan/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":80},"meta":{"digest":"2932b8cc09d6c0fe9439e5b642f4d0d80ecb38f61f5dca2662ffc65162d249a7","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-8k.6--plan/meta.json","size_bytes":719},"prompt":{"digest":"899e2eeda1055e5153408b6c9db896db02e6d0766c7cdfa8faebcdbda803ead0","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-8k.6--plan/prompt.md","size_bytes":178},"state":{"digest":"b63d12463bfcd220182fe6be40b9ec7e2769791553529f3188baf90bead6f584","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-8k.6--plan/state.json","size_bytes":180}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-8k.6--plan","local_name":"sase-8k.6--plan","metadata":{"agent_clan":"sase-8k","agent_clan_generation":"20260722105427","agent_family":"sase-8k.6","agent_family_role":"plan","approve":true,"bead_id":"sase-8k.6","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-8k","llm